# Cybersecurity Incident Analytics and Risk Assessment

## Project Overview

This project focuses on analysing cybersecurity incident data to support risk assessment, incident monitoring, and management decision-making. It uses spreadsheet data preparation, database information, calculations, and visualisations to turn raw data into useful insights.

## Objectives

- Improve data quality through data cleaning and validation.
- Analyse incident severity, status, risk scores, and resolution times.
- Organise related incident and device data using a data model.
- Present incident patterns and findings through charts, dashboards, and reports.
- Support cybersecurity decision-making with evidence-based recommendations.

## Tools and Technologies

- Microsoft Excel
- Power Query
- SQL and database data
- Data modelling and calculations
- PivotTables and PivotCharts
- Dashboard visualisation

## Project Activities

- Cleaned and prepared cybersecurity incident data for analysis.
- Worked with incident and related reference data.
- Organised data for analysis using relationships and calculations.
- Analysed incident severity, status, and risk-related information.
- Developed visual reports to communicate findings and support recommendations.

## Project Deliverables

- Prepared incident data
- Data model and calculations
- Incident analysis and visualisations
- Dashboard and management reporting
- Findings and recommended actions

## Key Learning Outcomes

This project develops practical skills in data preparation, analytical problem-solving, spreadsheet modelling, cybersecurity risk analysis, and communicating technical findings.

